    LLM: 'Game: Kwajongen. Logic: Partnership trick-taking. Key: 21-point threshold, branch-erasing scoring, Kapot bonus for all tricks.',
    Player: 'Kwajongen is a Flemish trick-taking game for 4 players in partnerships. 24-card deck (A-K-Q-J-10-9). Ace=4, King=3, Queen=2, Jack=1. Turned card is trump. Must win 21 of 40 points to erase a branch. First team to zero wins.',
    objective: 'Be the first team to reduce your starting score (e.g., 10 points) to zero.',
    gameplay: '1. Must follow suit if possible.\n2. Highest Trump wins the trick; otherwise, highest card of the led suit.\n3. **The Target**: Each round has 40 total points. The bidding team must win at least 21 points to reduce their score by 1 branch.',
